  "review": [
    {
      "section": "time.clock",
      "confidence": "low",
      "note": "Best effort per orchestrator instruction: 'awa {h}' (awa = hour, as the file's duration unit) + additive 'kɛ miniti N' (kɛ = and, miniti = minute). Minute numerals use the Mende vigesimal system: pu 10, pu mahu lɔɔlu 15, nuu yila gboyongo 20 ('one whole person'), ... nuu fele gboyongo 40, so 2:55 is long ('awa fele kɛ miniti nuu fele gboyongo mahu pu mahu lɔɔlu'). No half word used at 30 because the file's 'ta fele' could not be verified. Doubts: hour noun, the 'kɛ' linker, and whether speakers would really say such long minute counts rather than switch to Krio/English. Needs a Mende speaker."
    }
  ]
